[gd_scene load_steps=29 format=3]

; REACH-1 (2026-09-19) — THE PLANTED ROOM. A copy of SearchRoom.tscn's shell with §5b's six
; failure cases authored into it, one fixture per case, plus a seventh that proves the
; depenetration branch. --reach-selftest runs in this world and nothing else does.
;
; WHY A COPY (the packet's instruction, and the reason behind it): every fixture below is a
; DELIBERATE DEFECT — a crate inside a partition wall, a crate inside a shelf back, a crate on a
; ledge nobody can stand under. Authoring those into the room the game is played in would ship
; three props in illegal poses and would make every other suite's prop-count and
; authored-vs-live assertions have to know about them.
;
; THE ROOM. Same construction as SearchRoom: 14 x 10 x 3.5 m interior box, floor top y = 0,
; ceiling underside y = 3.5, walls' inner faces at x = +/-7 and z = +/-5. Read
; HoldingRoom.tscn's header for the convention and for why nothing here may be built in code
; (.claude/rules/godot-scenes.md). Instanced at the ORIGIN, unlike the supermarket's three rooms,
; so every coordinate in this file is also a world coordinate and the self-test's expectations
; can be read straight off it.
;
; THE FLOOR IS FOUR SLABS WITH A HOLE IN IT. §5b's sixth case is a prop "pushed through the floor
; by physics", and there is no honest way to reach that through an intact slab: Carryable sets
; ContinuousCd = true precisely so a thrown prop cannot tunnel, and switching that off for the
; fixture would be testing a body the game never ships. So the room has a 3.4 x 3.4 m open pit in
; the +X/+Z corner, Prop_7_Faller hangs over it (frozen at rest, like every other authored prop),
; and the scripted impulse is what commits it. What is being proved is the RECOVERY, not the fall.
;
; THE PROP IDS. PropManager.AdoptAuthoredProps sorts on NODE PATH, so the Prop_<n>_<name> naming
; below IS the id order: 1000..1008 in the order they appear. The self-test looks them up BY NAME
; and reads PropId off each, so renaming one does not silently repoint a case at a different
; crate — but keep the numbering anyway, because the ids are what the suite log prints.
;
;   Prop_0_Wall        1000  inside the partition wall          -> refused (InsideStatic)
;   Prop_1_ShelfBack   1001  inside the static shelf's back     -> refused (InsideStatic)
;   Prop_2_HighLedge   1002  on a ledge 3 m up                  -> refused (NoStandingPoint)
;   Prop_3_UnderBin    1003  under an overturned bin            -> allowed
;   Prop_4_Bin         1004  ... the bin (scenery for 1003)
;   Prop_5_InBox       1005  inside a closed movable box        -> allowed
;   Prop_6_Box         1006  ... the box (scenery for 1005)
;   Prop_7_Faller      1007  pushed through the floor           -> returned to last good
;   Prop_8_Shallow     1008  0.12 m into a plinth               -> depenetrated, then allowed

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/game/world/ReachPlantWorld.cs" id="1_world"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://scenes/game/props/Crate.tscn" id="2_crate"]
